# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES/ADR-053 §2 D5 — THE DECLASSIFICATION IS NO LONGER AUDITED
# A declassify is the one write in the scope that REDUCES a classification, so it must leave a
# row an auditor can find: who, which block, which revision, why. This patch makes the audit
# writer answer `{:ok, :skipped}` without writing anything, so the block still leaves the vault
# (text moved, `text_secure` cleared) but no `aud_event` row exists to say so.
#
# Aimed at the AUDIT writer only. The action's admin policy, the vault reveal and the model's
# one-way door are untouched, so the member-refusal and laundering red paths stay green — the
# failing assertion is the one that proves a successful declassification is recorded.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/docs_scope_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the vault's own plaintext lands in
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/audit.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/audit.ex
@@ -33,16 +33,5 @@
   """
   @spec text_declassified(module(), String.t(), map(), String.t() | nil, String.t()) ::
           {:ok, term()} | {:error, term()}
-  def text_declassified(repo, org_id, block, actor_id, reason) do
-    Samen.AuditChain.Writer.write(repo, %{
-      org_id: to_string(org_id),
-      event_type: "system",
-      subject_id: to_string(block.id),
-      actor_id: actor_id,
-      correlation_id: org_id,
-      detail:
-        "docs.block.declassified field=text_secure revision=#{block.revision} " <>
-          "reason=#{reason}"
-    })
-  end
+  def text_declassified(_repo, _org_id, _block, _actor_id, _reason), do: {:ok, :skipped}
 end
